# Build settings for the native app — the ONLY env files its build reads
# (svelte.config.js points SvelteKit's env dir here when OCHORUS_TARGET=app), so
# a web developer's frontend/.env can't leak into the app bundle. Every value
# here is PUBLIC (it ships in the website's bundle too), so it is committed.
# Local overrides go in app-env/.env.local (git-ignored); a real environment
# variable beats both, which is how `PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=… npm run app:build`
# points a build at a local API.
#
# Sign-in (MOBILE.md, "Sign-in in the app") turns on when BOTH Supabase values
# are set: the project URL (the one csp.config.js pins) and the anon /
# publishable key — the same public values as the website's
# PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL / PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY on Render. With either empty
# the app shows no sign-in and reads signed-out, as before.
#
# Not set on purpose: PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID (One Tap does not run in an app
# web view, and the app hides Google sign-in), PUBLIC_PLAUSIBLE_DOMAIN and
# PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN (app analytics and crash reporting are their own step).

PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://api.ochorus.com
PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://ochorus.com
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://eywunobxqijvwymdzlwy.supabase.co
# The anon / publishable key (public by design): Supabase → Project Settings →
# API keys, or the website's PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY on Render.
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
